=== TWHA902  gold 9 panels / Claude 4  (TWHA902 Be a Communicator.html)
   gold crumbs  : Introduction | Listening, speaking, reading, writing | Active listening | Body language | Using technology | Artistic expression | Feedback | The power of other languages | Know your audience | Ko tōku reo tōku ohooho. Ko tōku reo tōku māpihi maurea My language is my awakening. My language is the window to my soul. |  | Listening, speaking, reading, writing When we listen, speak, read and write well, we are more likely to get our message across clearly and accurately. This can have a positive impact on our relationships with others and help us to achieve new knowledge and skills we need in life. Let’s look more closely at each of these communication skills. Listening Listening is about holding attention for the speaker and putting our own thoughts aside to hear what the other person is trying to say. We will cover this more fully in the next lesson. Good listening helps us and those around us in lots of ways: It brings us closer together. It helps people feel seen and heard. It makes others feel valued and important. It prevents mistakes and confusion from happening. Speaking Speaking in a tone of voice that is clear, calm and confident can have a big impact. When you speak clearly to others, it helps them to understand the message you are trying to send them. If you think about what you want to say, before you say it, it also helps keep your message from being misheard or any confusion from the listener(s).
   Claude crumbs: Introduction | Listening, speaking, reading and writing well | Active listening | The power of other languages
